claim.claim-text:
receiving, from a host device (130; 250), a read command for a set of data (D0-D15) accessible by an interface controller (120; 230);
determining, based at least in part on the read command, that the set of data is absent from a buffer (170; 240; 340) coupled with the interface controller; and
sending, to the host device based at least in part on the set of data being absent from the buffer, an indication (420) of a time delay for the host device to observe before the host device issues a subsequent read command.

receiving, from a host device (130; 250), a write command for a set of data (D0-D15) provided to an interface controller (120; 230);
determining, based at least in part on the write command, a status of a buffer (240; 340) coupled with the interface controller; and
sending, to the host device based at least in part on the status of the buffer, an indication of a time delay for the host device to observe before the host device issues a subsequent write command.

a non-volatile memory (225; 325) coupled with an interface controller (120; 230);
a bus (110; 270) coupled with the interface controller, wherein the interface controller is configured to receive, from a host device (130; 250), an access command for a set of data associated with the non-volatile memory;
a buffer (240; 340) coupled with the interface controller, wherein the interface controller is configured to determine that the set of data is absent from the buffer; and
a pin coupled with the interface controller, wherein the interface controller is configured to send to the host device over the pin an indication that the set of data is absent from the buffer.
